# Expanded Test Data Seeding Plan

The goal is to expand the [seed_script.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/seed_script.js) to generate a larger, more diverse, and more realistic dataset for testing and demonstration purposes.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [seed_script.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/seed_script.js)

- **Year Expansion**: Increase the emission data range to 9 years (2016 - 2024).
- **Diverse Emission Types**:
    - **Scope 1**:
        - Stationary Combustion (Natural Gas, Diesel, Heavy Fuel Oil)
        - Mobile Combustion (Motor Gasoline, Diesel)
        - Fugitive Emissions (HFC-134a, Methane)
    - **Scope 2**:
        - Purchased Electricity
        - Purchased Steams/Heating
- **Profile-Based Seeding**:
    - Different facilities will have different dominant emission sources (e.g., a "Refinery" will have more Stationary Combustion, while an "Office" might have more Purchased Electricity).
- **Realistic Trends**:
    - Implement a simulated 2-3% year-over-year reduction in emissions to reflect corporate sustainability goals.
- **Goal Update**:
    - Seed `goals` for each of the 9 years to ensure the dashboard charts look complete.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `node seed_script.js`.
- Execute SQLite queries to verify counts:
    - `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM emissions;` (Expect ~540+ records for 5 facilities * 9 years * multiple types/months).
    - `SELECT DISTINCT year FROM emissions;` (Expect 9 distinct years).
    - `SELECT DISTINCT process_type FROM emissions;` (Expect 4+ distinct types).

### Manual Verification
- Log in as the `test` user.
- Verify the **Audit History** table displays entries.
- Verify the **Dashboard** charts (once navigated to) show the 9-year trend.
